module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Gluing
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.OpenImmersion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.GlobalGeneration
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Modules.ModuleGlueing.MatrixCocycle

/-!
# [Stacks, Tag 0B57] fails for a scheme that is not quasi-compact

[Stacks, Tag 0B57] states: for a morphism `X ⟶ Spec A`, a faithfully flat ring map `A ⟶ A'` and
a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F`, the module `F` is generated by global sections if and only if
its base change `F_{A'}` to `X_{A'} = X ×_{Spec A} Spec A'` is. The proof computes
`Γ(X_{A'}, F_{A'}) = Γ(X, F) ⊗_A A'` by [Stacks, Tag 02KH], which needs `X ⟶ Spec A` to be
quasi-compact and quasi-separated. This file shows that the equivalence fails for a scheme that is
not quasi-compact; the corrected statement, for `X ⟶ Spec A` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`.

## The counterexample

Take `A = ℤ` and `A' = ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`, the Zariski cover `D(3) ⊔ D(2)` of `Spec ℤ`. Glue

* the chart `Spec (ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3])`, two copies of `D(3)`, and
* for every `m`, the chart `Spec C_m` with `C_m = {(a, b) ∈ ℤ[1/2] × ℤ[1/2] | a ≡ b mod 3^m}`,
  two copies of `D(2)` glued at the prime `3` to order `m`,

all along `Spec (ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6])`, which is `D(2)` in the first chart and `D(3)` in each `C_m`.
The result `X` is two copies of `Spec ℤ`, kept apart over `D(3)` and identified at the prime `3`
by infinitely many charts, to every order; it is not quasi-compact. Let `W₁` be the first chart and
`W₂` the union of the others: `W₁ = X_3`, `W₂ = X_2`, and `W₁ ∩ W₂` is the overlap. Let `F` be the
invertible module which is trivial on `W₁` and on `W₂`, with transition function `ε = (2, 1)` on
the overlap.

* `F_{A'}` is generated by global sections: `X_{A'}` is the disjoint union of `X_3 = W₁` and
  `X_2 = W₂`, and `F` is trivial on each.
* `F` is not. A function on `W₂` restricts on the overlap to an element of every `C_m`, hence to a
  diagonal pair `(d, d)`: `ℤ[1/2]` has no nonzero element divisible by every power of `3`. A global
  section of `F` with coefficient `(a, b)` on `W₁` therefore has `(2a, b)` diagonal, so `b = 2a`,
  and it vanishes at the point `x₀` of `W₁` given by the prime `2` of the second factor.

So the global sections of `F` are the multiples of the section with coefficient `(1, 2)` on `W₁`,
and `Γ(X, F) ⊗ ℤ[1/3]` is not `Γ(X_3, F) = ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3]`: this is where 02KH, and with it the
proof of 0B57, fails for a scheme that is not quasi-compact.

## Main definitions

* `GlobalGenerationCounterexample.X`: the scheme `X`, as the colimit of the wide span of the
  charts over the overlap, in `Mathlib`'s locally directed gluing.
* `GlobalGenerationCounterexample.F`: the invertible module `F`, glued by
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.MatrixCocycle` from the transition function `ε`.
* `GlobalGenerationCounterexample.φ`: the faithfully flat ring map `ℤ ⟶ ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`.

## Main results

* `not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`: **[Stacks, Tag 0B57] is false
  as stated**, in the vocabulary of `nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`.
* `not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`: the same, in the vocabulary of
  `nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`.
* `GlobalGenerationCounterexample.not_nonempty_generatingSections_F`: `F` is not generated by
  global sections.
* `GlobalGenerationCounterexample.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_F`: its base change along
  `φ` is.
* `nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isCompl`: a pullback to a disjoint union of two opens
  is generated by global sections as soon as each open maps into an open over which one section
  generates every stalk.

## Implementation notes

Every chart ring is a subring of `ℚ × ℚ`, so all the comparison maps are inclusions and the
arithmetic happens in `ℚ`; the rings live in `ULift ℚ`, so that the counterexample exists in every
universe. The base `Spec ℤ` is `Spec (ULift ℤ)`, which is terminal, so the structure morphism
`X ⟶ Spec ℤ` is the unique one. The algebra `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]` is a product indexed by `Bool`, so
that its flatness follows from that of a finite direct sum.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B57](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B57)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02KH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange

/-! ### Global generation of a pullback to a disjoint union of two opens -/

section Clopen

variable {Y : Scheme.{u}} (N : Y.Modules)

/-- Any two sections of a sheaf of modules over an empty open agree. -/
lemma section_eq_of_eq_bot {W : Y.Opens} (hW : W = ⊥) (a b : ToType (N.val.presheaf.obj (op W))) :
    a = b := by
  let S : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} Y.carrier := ⟨N.val.presheaf, N.isSheaf⟩
  obtain ⟨_, -, hs⟩ := S.existsUnique_gluing' W (U := (Empty.elim : Empty → Y.Opens))
    (fun i => i.elim) (by rw [hW]; exact bot_le) (fun i => i.elim) (fun i => i.elim)
  exact (hs a (fun i => i.elim)).trans (hs b (fun i => i.elim)).symm

/-- A section of a sheaf of modules over one of two complementary opens extends, by zero on the
other, to a global section. -/
lemma exists_extend_of_isCompl {U₁ U₂ : Y.Opens} (hinf : U₁ ⊓ U₂ = ⊥) (hsup : U₁ ⊔ U₂ = ⊤)
    (τ : ToType (N.val.presheaf.obj (op U₁))) :
    ∃ σ : ToType (N.val.presheaf.obj (op ⊤)), N.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op σ = τ := by
  let S : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} Y.carrier := ⟨N.val.presheaf, N.isSheaf⟩
  let U : Bool → Y.Opens := fun b => cond b U₁ U₂
  let sf : ∀ b, ToType (S.1.obj (op (U b))) := fun b => match b with
    | true => τ
    | false => 0
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ, -⟩ := S.existsUnique_gluing' ⊤ (U := U) (fun _ => homOfLE le_top)
    (by rw [← hsup]; exact sup_le (le_iSup U true) (le_iSup U false)) sf (by
      intro i j
      cases i <;> cases j
      · rfl
      · exact section_eq_of_eq_bot N (by rwa [inf_comm]) _ _
      · exact section_eq_of_eq_bot N hinf _ _
      · rfl)
  exact ⟨σ, hσ true⟩

/-- **A pullback is generated by global sections at a point of one of two complementary opens**
`U ⊔ U' = ⊤`, `U ⊓ U' = ⊥` of the source, as soon as `U` maps into an open `V` over which one
section of the module generates every stalk. -/
lemma span_germTop_pullback_eq_top_of_isCompl {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ X) (M : X.Modules)
    {U U' : Y.Opens} (hinf : U ⊓ U' = ⊥) (hsup : U ⊔ U' = ⊤) {V : X.Opens} (hU : U ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ V)
    (s : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op V)))
    (hs : ∀ x (hx : x ∈ V), Submodule.span (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      {TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V x hx s} = ⊤)
    (y : Y) (hy : y ∈ U) :
    Submodule.span (R := ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y))
      (Set.range fun m : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj M, (⊤ : Y.Opens)) ↦
        germTop ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj M) y m) = ⊤ := by
  let : Algebra (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (p y))) (ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) :=
    (p.stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ :=
    RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.exists_modulePullbackStalkLinearEquiv p.toLRSHom.toShHom M y
  let P := (Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj M
  let τ : ToType (P.val.presheaf.obj (op U)) :=
    P.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE hU).op
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionsBaseChange.pullbackUnitSections p M V s)
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := exists_extend_of_isCompl P hinf hsup τ
  have hgerm : germTop P y σ = TopCat.Presheaf.germ P.val.presheaf (p ⁻¹ᵁ V) y (hU hy)
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionsBaseChange.pullbackUnitSections p M V s) := by
    show TopCat.Presheaf.germ P.val.presheaf ⊤ y trivial σ = _
    rw [← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply P.val.presheaf (homOfLE le_top) y hy σ, hσ]
    exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply P.val.presheaf (homOfLE hU) y hy _
  let e' : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) P.val.presheaf y)
      ≃ₗ[ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)]
      ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ⊗[ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (p y))]
        ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) M.val.presheaf (p y)) := e
  have he' : e' (germTop P y σ) = (1 : ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) ⊗ₜ[ToType
      (X.presheaf.stalk (p y))] TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V (p y) (hU hy) s := by
    rw [hgerm]
    exact he V (hU hy) s
  have htop : Submodule.span (ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) {e' (germTop P y σ)} = ⊤ := by
    suffices h : ∀ t, t ∈ Submodule.span (ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) {e' (germTop P y σ)} from
      eq_top_iff.mpr fun t _ => h t
    intro t
    induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero => exact zero_mem _
    | add t t' ht ht' => exact add_mem ht ht'
    | tmul a m =>
        obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp
          (show m ∈ Submodule.span _ _ from (hs (p y) (hU hy)).ge Submodule.mem_top)
        rw [he', ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, show (r • a) ⊗ₜ[ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (p y))]
            TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V (p y) (hU hy) s =
            (r • a) • ((1 : ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) ⊗ₜ[ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (p y))]
              TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V (p y) (hU hy) s) by
          rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_one]]
        exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  have hg : Submodule.span (ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) {germTop P y σ} = ⊤ := by
    have := congrArg (Submodule.map e'.symm.toLinearMap) htop
    rwa [Submodule.map_span, Set.image_singleton, LinearEquiv.coe_toLinearMap,
      LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply, Submodule.map_top, LinearEquiv.range] at this
  exact top_unique (hg.ge.trans (Submodule.span_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr ⟨σ, rfl⟩)))

/-- **A pullback to a disjoint union of two opens is generated by global sections** as soon as
each of the two opens maps into an open over which one section of the module generates every
stalk. -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isCompl {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ X)
    (M : X.Modules) {U₁ U₂ : Y.Opens} (hinf : U₁ ⊓ U₂ = ⊥) (hsup : U₁ ⊔ U₂ = ⊤)
    {V₁ V₂ : X.Opens} (hU₁ : U₁ ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ V₁) (hU₂ : U₂ ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)
    (s₁ : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op V₁))) (s₂ : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op V₂)))
    (hs₁ : ∀ x (hx : x ∈ V₁), Submodule.span (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      {TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V₁ x hx s₁} = ⊤)
    (hs₂ : ∀ x (hx : x ∈ V₂), Submodule.span (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      {TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf V₂ x hx s₂} = ⊤) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj M).GeneratingSections := by
  refine nonempty_generatingSections_of_span_germTop_eq_top _ fun y => ?_
  rcases (show y ∈ U₁ ⊔ U₂ from hsup ▸ trivial) with hy | hy
  · exact span_germTop_pullback_eq_top_of_isCompl p M hinf hsup hU₁ s₁ hs₁ y hy
  · exact span_germTop_pullback_eq_top_of_isCompl p M (by rwa [inf_comm])
      (by rwa [sup_comm]) hU₂ s₂ hs₂ y hy

end Clopen

namespace GlobalGenerationCounterexample

/-! ### The rings -/

/-- The field `ℚ`, in universe `u`. -/
abbrev K : Type u := ULift.{u} ℚ

/-- The subring `ℤ[1/p]` of `ℚ`. -/
def zInv (p : ℕ) : Subring K.{u} where
  carrier := {q | ∃ n : ℕ, ∃ z : ℤ, q.down * (p : ℚ) ^ n = z}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨n, z, hz⟩ ⟨n', z', hz'⟩
    refine ⟨n + n', z * z', ?_⟩
    simp only [ULift.mul_down, Int.cast_mul, ← hz, ← hz', pow_add]
    ring
  one_mem' := ⟨0, 1, by simp⟩
  add_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨n, z, hz⟩ ⟨n', z', hz'⟩
    refine ⟨n + n', z * p ^ n' + z' * p ^ n, ?_⟩
    simp only [ULift.add_down, Int.cast_add, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_pow, Int.cast_natCast, ← hz,
      ← hz', pow_add]
    ring
  zero_mem' := ⟨0, 0, by simp⟩
  neg_mem' := by
    rintro a ⟨n, z, hz⟩
    exact ⟨n, -z, by simp [← hz]⟩

/-- `ℤ[1/p] ⊆ ℤ[1/6]` for `p ∣ 6`. -/
lemma zInv_le_six {p : ℕ} (hp : p ∣ 6) : zInv.{u} p ≤ zInv 6 := by
  rintro q ⟨n, z, hz⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hp
  refine ⟨n, z * c ^ n, ?_⟩
  simp [hc, mul_pow, ← hz, mul_assoc]

/-- The ring `ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6]` of the overlap. -/
def ringL : Subring (K.{u} × K.{u}) := (zInv 6).prod (zInv 6)

/-- The ring `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3]` of the chart over `D(3)`. -/
def ringR : Subring (K.{u} × K.{u}) := (zInv 3).prod (zInv 3)

/-- The ring `{(a, b) ∈ ℤ[1/2] × ℤ[1/2] | a ≡ b mod 3^m}` of the `m`-th chart over `D(2)`: two
copies of `Spec ℤ[1/2]` glued at the prime `3` to order `m`. -/
def ringC (m : ℕ) : Subring (K.{u} × K.{u}) where
  carrier := {x | x.1 ∈ zInv 2 ∧ x.2 ∈ zInv 2 ∧ ∃ y ∈ zInv 2, x.1 - x.2 = 3 ^ m * y}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨ha1, ha2, y, hy, hay⟩ ⟨hb1, hb2, y', hy', hby⟩
    refine ⟨mul_mem ha1 hb1, mul_mem ha2 hb2, a.1 * y' + b.2 * y,
      add_mem (mul_mem ha1 hy') (mul_mem hb2 hy), ?_⟩
    simp only [Prod.fst_mul, Prod.snd_mul]
    linear_combination a.1 * hby + b.2 * hay
  one_mem' := ⟨one_mem _, one_mem _, 0, zero_mem _, by simp⟩
  add_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨ha1, ha2, y, hy, hay⟩ ⟨hb1, hb2, y', hy', hby⟩
    refine ⟨add_mem ha1 hb1, add_mem ha2 hb2, y + y', add_mem hy hy', ?_⟩
    simp only [Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add]
    linear_combination hay + hby
  zero_mem' := ⟨zero_mem _, zero_mem _, 0, zero_mem _, by simp⟩
  neg_mem' := by
    rintro a ⟨ha1, ha2, y, hy, hay⟩
    refine ⟨neg_mem ha1, neg_mem ha2, -y, neg_mem hy, ?_⟩
    simp only [Prod.fst_neg, Prod.snd_neg]
    linear_combination -hay

/-- `ℤ[1/3]² ⊆ ℤ[1/6]²`. -/
lemma ringR_le_ringL : ringR.{u} ≤ ringL := fun _ hx =>
  ⟨zInv_le_six (by norm_num) hx.1, zInv_le_six (by norm_num) hx.2⟩

/-- `C_m ⊆ ℤ[1/6]²`. -/
lemma ringC_le_ringL (m : ℕ) : ringC.{u} m ≤ ringL := fun _ hx =>
  ⟨zInv_le_six (by norm_num) hx.1, zInv_le_six (by norm_num) hx.2.1⟩

/-- `ℤ[1/6]²` as an algebra over `ℤ[1/3]²`, by inclusion. -/
instance : Algebra ringR.{u} ringL.{u} := (Subring.inclusion ringR_le_ringL).toAlgebra

/-- `ℤ[1/6]²` as an algebra over `C_m`, by inclusion. -/
instance (m : ℕ) : Algebra (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u} :=
  (Subring.inclusion (ringC_le_ringL m)).toAlgebra

/-- A divisor of `6` is invertible in `ℤ[1/6]²`. -/
lemma isUnit_ringL {p : ℕ} (hp : p ∣ 6) (hp0 : p ≠ 0) : IsUnit (p : ringL.{u}) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hp
  refine isUnit_iff_exists_inv.mpr ⟨⟨((⟨(p : ℚ)⁻¹⟩ : K), (⟨(p : ℚ)⁻¹⟩ : K)), ?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · exact ⟨1, c, by simp [hc]; field_simp⟩
  · exact ⟨1, c, by simp [hc]; field_simp⟩
  · apply Subtype.ext
    apply Prod.ext <;> apply ULift.ext <;> simp [hp0]

/-- A denominator-power of `6` can be split off: `q · 2^n ∈ ℤ[1/3]` and `q · 3^n ∈ ℤ[1/2]` for
every large `n`. -/
lemma mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six {q : K.{u}} (h : q ∈ zInv 6) :
    ∃ N, ∀ n ≥ N, q * 2 ^ n ∈ zInv 3 ∧ q * 3 ^ n ∈ zInv 2 := by
  obtain ⟨N, z, hz⟩ := h
  have hz' : q.down * 6 ^ N = z := by exact_mod_cast hz
  refine ⟨N, fun n hn => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le hn
  refine ⟨⟨N + k, z * 6 ^ k, ?_⟩, ⟨N + k, z * 6 ^ k, ?_⟩⟩ <;>
  · simp only [ULift.mul_down, ULift.pow_down, ULift.down_ofNat]
    push_cast
    rw [← hz', show (6 : ℚ) = 2 * 3 by norm_num, mul_pow, mul_pow]
    ring

/-- `ℤ[1/6]² = (ℤ[1/3]²)[1/2]`: the overlap is `D(2)` in the first chart. -/
instance : IsLocalization.Away (2 : ringR.{u}) ringL.{u} where
  map_units := by
    rintro ⟨_, n, rfl⟩
    rw [map_pow, map_ofNat]
    exact (isUnit_ringL.{u} (p := 2) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)).pow n
  surj := by
    rintro ⟨z, h1, h2⟩
    obtain ⟨N1, hN1⟩ := mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six h1
    obtain ⟨N2, hN2⟩ := mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six h2
    exact ⟨⟨⟨z * 2 ^ (N1 + N2), (hN1 _ (by omega)).1, (hN2 _ (by omega)).1⟩,
      ⟨2 ^ (N1 + N2), N1 + N2, rfl⟩⟩, rfl⟩
  exists_of_eq h := ⟨1, by simpa using Subring.inclusion_injective ringR_le_ringL h⟩

/-- `ℤ[1/6]² = C_m[1/3]`: the overlap is `D(3)` in the chart `Spec C_m`. -/
instance (m : ℕ) : IsLocalization.Away (3 : ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u} where
  map_units := by
    rintro ⟨_, n, rfl⟩
    rw [map_pow, map_ofNat]
    exact (isUnit_ringL.{u} (p := 3) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)).pow n
  surj := by
    rintro ⟨z, h1, h2⟩
    obtain ⟨N1, hN1⟩ := mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six h1
    obtain ⟨N2, hN2⟩ := mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six h2
    obtain ⟨N3, hN3⟩ := mul_pow_mem_of_mem_zInv_six (sub_mem h1 h2)
    refine ⟨⟨⟨z * 3 ^ (N1 + N2 + N3 + m), (hN1 _ (by omega)).2, (hN2 _ (by omega)).2,
      (z.1 - z.2) * 3 ^ (N1 + N2 + N3), (hN3 _ (by omega)).2, ?_⟩,
      ⟨3 ^ (N1 + N2 + N3 + m), N1 + N2 + N3 + m, rfl⟩⟩, rfl⟩
    simp only [Prod.fst_mul, Prod.snd_mul, Prod.pow_fst, Prod.pow_snd, Prod.fst_ofNat,
      Prod.snd_ofNat, pow_add]
    ring
  exists_of_eq h := ⟨1, by simpa using Subring.inclusion_injective (ringC_le_ringL m) h⟩

/-! ### The arithmetic -/

/-- An integer divisible by every power of `3` is zero. -/
lemma int_eq_zero_of_forall_dvd {z : ℤ} (h : ∀ m : ℕ, (3 : ℤ) ^ m ∣ z) : z = 0 := by
  by_contra hz
  have hlt : z.natAbs < 3 ^ z.natAbs := Nat.lt_pow_self (by norm_num)
  have hd : 3 ^ z.natAbs ∣ z.natAbs := by
    simpa [Int.natAbs_pow] using Int.natAbs_dvd_natAbs.mpr (h z.natAbs)
  have := Nat.le_of_dvd (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hz) hd
  omega

/-- A rational number lying in `3^m ℤ[1/2]` for every `m` is zero. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_forall_mem_pow_three_mul {q : K.{u}}
    (h : ∀ m : ℕ, ∃ y ∈ zInv 2, q = 3 ^ m * y) : q = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨n, z, hz⟩ : q ∈ zInv 2 := by
    obtain ⟨y₀, hy₀, hq⟩ := h 0
    rw [hq, pow_zero, one_mul]
    exact hy₀
  have hz' : q.down * 2 ^ n = z := by exact_mod_cast hz
  suffices hz0 : z = 0 by
    apply ULift.ext
    rw [hz0, Int.cast_zero] at hz'
    exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hz').resolve_right (pow_ne_zero _ (by norm_num))
  refine int_eq_zero_of_forall_dvd fun m => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, ⟨k, w, hw⟩, hy⟩ := h m
  have hw' : y.down * 2 ^ k = w := by exact_mod_cast hw
  have hcop : IsCoprime ((3 : ℤ) ^ m) (2 ^ k) :=
    IsCoprime.pow (⟨1, -1, by norm_num⟩ : IsCoprime (3 : ℤ) 2)
  refine hcop.dvd_of_dvd_mul_right ⟨w * 2 ^ n, ?_⟩
  have : ((z * 2 ^ k : ℤ) : ℚ) = ((3 ^ m * (w * 2 ^ n) : ℤ) : ℚ) := by
    push_cast
    rw [← hw', ← hz', hy]
    simp only [ULift.mul_down, ULift.pow_down, ULift.down_ofNat]
    ring
  exact_mod_cast this

/-- An element of `ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6]` lying in every `C_m` is diagonal. -/
lemma fst_eq_snd_of_forall_mem_ringC {ℓ : ringL.{u}}
    (h : ∀ m : ℕ, ∃ c : ringC.{u} m, algebraMap _ _ c = ℓ) :
    (ℓ : K.{u} × K.{u}).1 = (ℓ : K.{u} × K.{u}).2 := by
  refine sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_forall_mem_pow_three_mul fun m => ?_)
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h m
  obtain ⟨-, -, y, hy, hc'⟩ := c.2
  refine ⟨y, hy, ?_⟩
  rw [← hc]
  exact hc'

/-- The prime `P` of `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3]`: the prime `2` of the second factor. -/
def idealP : Ideal ringR.{u} where
  carrier := {r | ∃ y ∈ zInv 3, (r : K.{u} × K.{u}).2 = 2 * y}
  add_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨y, hy, ha⟩ ⟨y', hy', hb⟩
    exact ⟨y + y', add_mem hy hy', by simp only [Subring.coe_add, Prod.snd_add, ha, hb]; ring⟩
  zero_mem' := ⟨0, zero_mem _, by simp⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c a ⟨y, hy, ha⟩
    exact ⟨(c : K × K).2 * y, mul_mem c.2.2 hy, by
      simp only [smul_eq_mul, Subring.coe_mul, Prod.snd_mul, ha]; ring⟩

/-- `x / 3^n ∈ 2 ℤ[1/3]` exactly when `2 ∣ x`. -/
lemma two_mul_mem_zInv_three_iff {x : ℤ} {n : ℕ} :
    (∃ y ∈ zInv.{u} 3, (⟨(x : ℚ) / 3 ^ n⟩ : K.{u}) = 2 * y) ↔ (2 : ℤ) ∣ x := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, ⟨k, w, hw⟩, hy⟩
    have h1 : (x : ℚ) * 3 ^ k = 2 * w * 3 ^ n := by
      have := congrArg ULift.down hy
      simp only [ULift.mul_down, ULift.down_ofNat] at this
      rw [← hw]
      field_simp at this ⊢
      rw [this]
      ring
    have hcop : IsCoprime (2 : ℤ) (3 ^ k) :=
      IsCoprime.pow_right (⟨-1, 1, by norm_num⟩ : IsCoprime (2 : ℤ) 3)
    exact hcop.dvd_of_dvd_mul_right ⟨w * 3 ^ n, by rw [← mul_assoc]; exact_mod_cast h1⟩
  · rintro ⟨t, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨⟨(t : ℚ) / 3 ^ n⟩, ⟨n, t, by simp⟩, ?_⟩
    apply ULift.ext
    simp only [ULift.mul_down, ULift.down_ofNat, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_ofNat]
    ring

/-- Every element of `ℤ[1/3]` is `x / 3^n` with `x ∈ ℤ`. -/
lemma exists_eq_div_of_mem_zInv_three {q : K.{u}} (h : q ∈ zInv 3) :
    ∃ x : ℤ, ∃ n : ℕ, q = ⟨(x : ℚ) / 3 ^ n⟩ := by
  obtain ⟨n, x, hx⟩ := h
  refine ⟨x, n, ULift.ext _ _ ?_⟩
  simp only [Nat.cast_ofNat] at hx
  rw [← hx]
  field_simp

/-- `P` is prime, `2` being prime in `ℤ[1/3]`. -/
instance : idealP.{u}.IsPrime where
  ne_top' := by
    intro htop
    obtain ⟨y, hy, h1⟩ : (1 : ringR.{u}) ∈ idealP := htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top
    have h1' : (⟨((1 : ℤ) : ℚ) / 3 ^ 0⟩ : K.{u}) = 2 * y := by
      refine Eq.trans ?_ h1
      apply ULift.ext
      simp
    have := (two_mul_mem_zInv_three_iff.{u} (x := 1) (n := 0)).mp ⟨y, hy, h1'⟩
    norm_num at this
  mem_or_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨y, hy, hab⟩
    obtain ⟨x, n, hxa⟩ := exists_eq_div_of_mem_zInv_three a.2.2
    obtain ⟨x', n', hxb⟩ := exists_eq_div_of_mem_zInv_three b.2.2
    have hprod : (⟨((x * x' : ℤ) : ℚ) / 3 ^ (n + n')⟩ : K.{u}) = 2 * y := by
      rw [← hab]
      simp only [Subring.coe_mul, Prod.snd_mul, hxa, hxb]
      apply ULift.ext
      simp only [ULift.mul_down, Int.cast_mul, pow_add]
      field_simp
    have h2 := (two_mul_mem_zInv_three_iff.{u}).mp ⟨y, hy, hprod⟩
    rcases (Int.prime_two.dvd_mul).mp h2 with h | h
    · left
      have := (two_mul_mem_zInv_three_iff.{u} (n := n)).mpr h
      rw [← hxa] at this
      exact this
    · right
      have := (two_mul_mem_zInv_three_iff.{u} (n := n')).mpr h
      rw [← hxb] at this
      exact this

/-! ### The scheme -/

/-- The overlap `Spec (ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6])`. -/
abbrev specL : Scheme.{u} := Spec (CommRingCat.of ringL.{u})

/-- The charts: `Spec (ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3])` over `D(3)`, and `Spec C_m` over `D(2)`. -/
def chart : Option ℕ → Scheme.{u}
  | none => Spec (CommRingCat.of ringR.{u})
  | some m => Spec (CommRingCat.of (ringC.{u} m))

/-- The overlap inside each chart, as the spectrum of a localization. -/
def chartArrow : (j : Option ℕ) → specL.{u} ⟶ chart j
  | none => Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ringR.{u} ringL.{u}))
  | some m => Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u}))

/-- The overlap is an open subscheme of each chart. -/
instance isOpenImmersion_chartArrow (j : Option ℕ) : IsOpenImmersion (chartArrow.{u} j) := by
  cases j with
  | none => exact IsOpenImmersion.of_isLocalization (2 : ringR.{u})
  | some m => exact IsOpenImmersion.of_isLocalization (3 : ringC.{u} m)

/-- The diagram of open immersions from the overlap to the charts. -/
def diagram : WidePushoutShape (Option ℕ) ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  WidePushoutShape.wideSpan specL chart chartArrow

/-- Every map of the diagram is an open immersion. -/
instance {i j : WidePushoutShape (Option ℕ)} (f : i ⟶ j) : IsOpenImmersion (diagram.{u}.map f) := by
  cases f with
  | id => exact IsOpenImmersion.of_isIso (𝟙 (diagram.{u}.obj i))
  | init j => exact isOpenImmersion_chartArrow j

/-- The index category is small, so that the colimit is a scheme in universe `u`. -/
instance : Small.{u} (WidePushoutShape (Option ℕ)) :=
  small_map (Equiv.refl (Option (Option ℕ)) : WidePushoutShape (Option ℕ) ≃ Option (Option ℕ))

/-- **The scheme `X`**: two copies of `Spec ℤ`, kept apart over `D(3)` and identified over the
prime `3` by infinitely many charts, the `m`-th of them to order `m`. -/
def X : Scheme.{u} := colimit diagram.{u}

/-- The overlap, as an open subscheme of `X`. -/
def ιV : specL.{u} ⟶ X.{u} := colimit.ι diagram.{u} none

/-- The chart `Spec (ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3])` of `X`. -/
def ιR : Spec (CommRingCat.of ringR.{u}) ⟶ X.{u} := colimit.ι diagram.{u} (some none)

/-- The `m`-th chart `Spec C_m` of `X`. -/
def ιC (m : ℕ) : Spec (CommRingCat.of (ringC.{u} m)) ⟶ X.{u} :=
  colimit.ι diagram.{u} (some (some m))

/-- The overlap is an open subscheme of `X`. -/
instance : IsOpenImmersion ιV.{u} :=
  (inferInstance : IsOpenImmersion (colimit.ι diagram.{u} none))
/-- The first chart is an open subscheme of `X`. -/
instance : IsOpenImmersion ιR.{u} :=
  (inferInstance : IsOpenImmersion (colimit.ι diagram.{u} (some none)))
/-- Each chart `Spec C_m` is an open subscheme of `X`. -/
instance (m : ℕ) : IsOpenImmersion (ιC.{u} m) :=
  (inferInstance : IsOpenImmersion (colimit.ι diagram.{u} (some (some m))))

/-- The overlap maps to `X` through the first chart. -/
lemma arrowR_ιR :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ringR.{u} ringL.{u})) ≫ ιR.{u} = ιV :=
  colimit.w diagram.{u} (WidePushoutShape.Hom.init none)

/-- The overlap maps to `X` through each chart `Spec C_m`. -/
lemma arrowC_ιC (m : ℕ) :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u})) ≫ ιC.{u} m = ιV :=
  colimit.w diagram.{u} (WidePushoutShape.Hom.init (some m))

/-- `arrowR_ιR` on points. -/
lemma ιR_apply_arrow (z : specL.{u}) :
    ιR (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ringR.{u} ringL.{u})) z) = ιV z :=
  (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ z).symm.trans (by rw [arrowR_ιR])

/-- `arrowC_ιC` on points. -/
lemma ιC_apply_arrow (m : ℕ) (z : specL.{u}) :
    ιC m (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u})) z) = ιV z :=
  (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ z).symm.trans (by rw [arrowC_ιC])

/-- The open `W₁ = X_3`: the chart `Spec (ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3])`. -/
def W₁ : X.{u}.Opens := ιR.opensRange

/-- The open `W₂ = X_2`: the union of the charts `Spec C_m`. -/
def W₂ : X.{u}.Opens := ⨆ m, (ιC.{u} m).opensRange

/-- The overlap `W₁ ∩ W₂`. -/
abbrev Vo : X.{u}.Opens := ιV ''ᵁ ⊤

/-- The points of the overlap. -/
lemma mem_Vo {x : X.{u}} : x ∈ Vo ↔ ∃ z, ιV z = x :=
  ⟨fun ⟨z, _, hz⟩ => ⟨z, hz⟩, fun ⟨z, hz⟩ => ⟨z, trivial, hz⟩⟩

/-- The overlap lies in `W₁`. -/
lemma Vo_le_W₁ : Vo.{u} ≤ W₁ := by
  rintro _ ⟨z, -, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨_, ιR_apply_arrow z⟩

/-- The overlap lies in each chart `Spec C_m`. -/
lemma Vo_le_rangeC (m : ℕ) : Vo.{u} ≤ (ιC.{u} m).opensRange := by
  rintro _ ⟨z, -, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨_, ιC_apply_arrow m z⟩

/-- Each chart `Spec C_m` lies in `W₂`. -/
lemma rangeC_le_W₂ (m : ℕ) : (ιC.{u} m).opensRange ≤ W₂ := le_iSup (fun m => (ιC m).opensRange) m

/-- The overlap lies in `W₂`. -/
lemma Vo_le_W₂ : Vo.{u} ≤ W₂ := (Vo_le_rangeC 0).trans (rangeC_le_W₂ 0)

/-- **`W₁ ∩ W₂` is the overlap**: a point of the first chart and of a chart `Spec C_m` comes
from the overlap, since the diagram is locally directed. -/
lemma W₁_inf_W₂ : W₁.{u} ⊓ W₂ ≤ Vo := by
  rintro x ⟨⟨a, rfl⟩, hx⟩
  obtain ⟨m, b, hb⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp hx
  have := (Scheme.IsLocallyDirected.ι_eq_ι_iff diagram.{u}).mp hb.symm
  obtain ⟨k, fi, fj, z, hz, -⟩ := this
  cases fi with
  | id => cases fj
  | init j =>
      refine mem_Vo.mpr ⟨z, ?_⟩
      rw [← hz]
      exact (ιR_apply_arrow z).symm

/-- `W₁` and `W₂` cover `X`. -/
lemma W₁_sup_W₂ : W₁.{u} ⊔ W₂ = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := Scheme.IsLocallyDirected.ι_jointly_surjective diagram.{u} x
  rcases i with _ | _ | m
  · exact Or.inl (Vo_le_W₁ (mem_Vo.mpr ⟨y, rfl⟩))
  · exact Or.inl ⟨y, rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inr (rangeC_le_W₂ m ⟨y, rfl⟩)

/-- A point of a chart at which `n` is invertible lies in the overlap, when the overlap is
the localization of the chart at `n`. -/
private lemma mem_Vo_of_mem_basicOpen {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [Algebra R ringL.{u}] (n : ℕ)
    [n.AtLeastTwo] [IsLocalization.Away (OfNat.ofNat n : R) ringL.{u}]
    (ι : Spec (CommRingCat.of R) ⟶ X.{u})
    (h : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R ringL.{u})) ≫ ι = ιV)
    (y : Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) (hy : ι y ∈ X.{u}.basicOpen (OfNat.ofNat n : Γ(X.{u}, ⊤))) :
    ι y ∈ Vo.{u} := by
  have hy : y ∈ ι ⁻¹ᵁ X.{u}.basicOpen (OfNat.ofNat n : Γ(X.{u}, ⊤)) := hy
  rw [Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top, map_ofNat, basicOpen_eq_of_affine', map_ofNat] at hy
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ : ∃ z : specL.{u},
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R ringL.{u})) z = y := by
    have : (y : PrimeSpectrum R) ∈ Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap R ringL.{u})) := by
      rw [PrimeSpectrum.localization_away_comap_range ringL.{u} (OfNat.ofNat n : R)]
      exact hy
    exact this
  refine mem_Vo.mpr ⟨z, ?_⟩
  rw [← h]
  exact (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ z).trans (congrArg ι hz)

/-- `X_3 ⊆ W₁`: a point of a chart `Spec C_m` at which `3` is invertible lies in the overlap. -/
lemma basicOpen_three_le_W₁ : X.{u}.basicOpen (3 : Γ(X.{u}, ⊤)) ≤ W₁ := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := Scheme.IsLocallyDirected.ι_jointly_surjective diagram.{u} x
  rcases i with _ | _ | m
  · exact Vo_le_W₁ (mem_Vo.mpr ⟨y, rfl⟩)
  · exact ⟨y, rfl⟩
  · exact Vo_le_W₁ (mem_Vo_of_mem_basicOpen 3 (ιC m) (arrowC_ιC m) y hx)

/-- `X_2 ⊆ W₂`: a point of the chart `Spec (ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3])` at which `2` is invertible lies in
the overlap. -/
lemma basicOpen_two_le_W₂ : X.{u}.basicOpen (2 : Γ(X.{u}, ⊤)) ≤ W₂ := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := Scheme.IsLocallyDirected.ι_jointly_surjective diagram.{u} x
  rcases i with _ | _ | m
  · exact Vo_le_W₂ (mem_Vo.mpr ⟨y, rfl⟩)
  · exact Vo_le_W₂ (mem_Vo_of_mem_basicOpen 2 ιR arrowR_ιR y hx)
  · exact rangeC_le_W₂ m ⟨y, rfl⟩

/-! ### Reading functions in the charts -/

/-- The overlap maps into any open containing it. -/
lemma top_le_preimage_of_Vo_le {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : Vo ≤ U) : ⊤ ≤ ιV ⁻¹ᵁ U :=
  fun z _ => h (mem_Vo.mpr ⟨z, rfl⟩)

/-- The first chart maps into any open containing it. -/
lemma top_le_preimage_of_W₁_le {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W₁ ≤ U) : ⊤ ≤ ιR ⁻¹ᵁ U :=
  fun z _ => h ⟨z, rfl⟩

/-- A chart `Spec C_m` maps into any open containing it. -/
lemma top_le_preimage_of_rangeC_le {m : ℕ} {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : (ιC m).opensRange ≤ U) :
    ⊤ ≤ ιC m ⁻¹ᵁ U :=
  fun z _ => h ⟨z, rfl⟩

/-- A function on an open containing the overlap, read in `ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6]`. -/
def readV {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : Vo ≤ U) : Γ(X.{u}, U) →+* ringL.{u} :=
  (ιV.appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_Vo_le h) ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom).hom

/-- A function on an open containing `W₁`, read in `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3]`. -/
def readR {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W₁ ≤ U) : Γ(X.{u}, U) →+* ringR.{u} :=
  (ιR.appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_W₁_le h) ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom).hom

/-- A function on an open containing the `m`-th chart, read in `C_m`. -/
def readC (m : ℕ) {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : (ιC m).opensRange ≤ U) : Γ(X.{u}, U) →+* ringC.{u} m :=
  ((ιC m).appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_rangeC_le h) ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom).hom

/-- Pulling functions back to the whole source along a composite. -/
lemma appLE_top_of_comp_eq {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} {g : Z ⟶ Y} {f : Y ⟶ X} {k : Z ⟶ X}
    (hk : g ≫ f = k) (U : X.Opens) (e : ⊤ ≤ k ⁻¹ᵁ U) (e' : ⊤ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U) :
    k.appLE U ⊤ e = f.appLE U ⊤ e' ≫ g.appLE ⊤ ⊤ le_top := by
  subst hk
  exact (Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE g f U ⊤ ⊤ e' le_top).symm

/-- `Spec.map φ` on global functions is `φ`. -/
lemma SpecMap_appLE_top_ΓSpecIso {R S : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : R ⟶ S) :
    (Spec.map φ).appLE ⊤ ⊤ le_top ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso S).hom = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).hom ≫ φ := by
  rw [← Scheme.ΓSpecIso_naturality]
  congr 1

/-- A function on an open containing `W₁`, read in the overlap, is the image of its reading
in the first chart. -/
lemma readV_eq_readR {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W₁ ≤ U) (c : Γ(X.{u}, U)) :
    readV (Vo_le_W₁.trans h) c = algebraMap ringR.{u} ringL.{u} (readR h c) := by
  have key : ιV.appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_Vo_le (Vo_le_W₁.trans h)) ≫
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom = ιR.appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_W₁_le h) ≫
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap ringR.{u} ringL.{u}) := by
    rw [appLE_top_of_comp_eq arrowR_ιR U _ (top_le_preimage_of_W₁_le h), Category.assoc,
      SpecMap_appLE_top_ΓSpecIso]
  exact congrArg (fun φ => φ.hom c) key

/-- A function on an open containing `Spec C_m`, read in the overlap, is the image of its
reading in `C_m`. -/
lemma readV_eq_readC (m : ℕ) {U : X.{u}.Opens} (h : (ιC m).opensRange ≤ U) (c : Γ(X.{u}, U)) :
    readV ((Vo_le_rangeC m).trans h) c = algebraMap (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u} (readC m h c) := by
  have key : ιV.appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_Vo_le ((Vo_le_rangeC m).trans h)) ≫
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom = (ιC m).appLE U ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_rangeC_le h) ≫
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (ringC.{u} m) ringL.{u}) := by
    rw [appLE_top_of_comp_eq (arrowC_ιC m) U _ (top_le_preimage_of_rangeC_le h),
      Category.assoc, SpecMap_appLE_top_ΓSpecIso]
  exact congrArg (fun φ => φ.hom c) key

/-- Reading in the overlap commutes with restriction. -/
lemma readV_res {U U' : X.{u}.Opens} (h : Vo ≤ U') (hU : U' ≤ U) (c : Γ(X.{u}, U)) :
    readV h (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hU).op c) = readV (h.trans hU) c := by
  simp only [readV]
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Category.assoc, Scheme.Hom.map_appLE]

/-! ### The line bundle -/

/-- The transition function `(2, 1)` of the line bundle, as an element of `ℤ[1/6] × ℤ[1/6]`. -/
def ε₀ : ringL.{u} := ⟨(2, 1), ⟨0, 2, by simp⟩, ⟨0, 1, by simp⟩⟩

/-- The inverse `(1/2, 1)` of `ε₀`. -/
def ε₀' : ringL.{u} := ⟨(⟨1 / 2⟩, 1), ⟨1, 3, by norm_num⟩, ⟨0, 1, by simp⟩⟩

/-- `ε₀ ε₀' = 1`. -/
lemma ε₀_mul_ε₀' : ε₀.{u} * ε₀' = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply Prod.ext <;> apply ULift.ext <;> norm_num [ε₀, ε₀']

/-- The transition function on the overlap. -/
def ε : Γ(X.{u}, Vo) := (ιV.appIso ⊤).inv.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv.hom ε₀)

/-- Its inverse. -/
def ε' : Γ(X.{u}, Vo) := (ιV.appIso ⊤).inv.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv.hom ε₀')

/-- `ε ε' = 1`. -/
lemma ε_mul_ε' : ε.{u} * ε' = 1 := by
  rw [ε, ε', ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ε₀_mul_ε₀', map_one, map_one]

/-- `ε`, read in the overlap, is `(2, 1)`. -/
lemma readV_ε : readV.{u} le_rfl ε = ε₀ := by
  have h1 : (ιV.appIso ⊤).inv ≫ ιV.appLE Vo ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_Vo_le le_rfl) = 𝟙 _ := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appIso_inv_appLE]
    exact specL.presheaf.map_id _
  show ((ιV.appIso ⊤).inv ≫ ιV.appLE Vo ⊤ _ ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).hom).hom
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv.hom ε₀) = ε₀
  rw [← Category.assoc, h1, Category.id_comp]
  exact Iso.inv_hom_id_apply (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of ringL.{u})) ε₀

/-- `ε`, as a section of the sheaf of rings `X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
def εR : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op Vo)) := ε

/-- `ε'`, as a section of the sheaf of rings `X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
def εR' : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op Vo)) := ε'

/-- `ε ε' = 1` in `X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
lemma εR_mul_εR' : εR.{u} * εR' = 1 := ε_mul_ε'

/-- `ε' ε = 1` in `X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
lemma εR'_mul_εR : εR'.{u} * εR = 1 := (mul_comm ε' ε).trans ε_mul_ε'

/-- The two members `W₁`, `W₂` of the trivialising cover. -/
def Wk : ULift.{u} Bool → X.{u}.Opens
  | ⟨true⟩ => W₁
  | ⟨false⟩ => W₂

/-- `W₁` and `W₂` cover `X`, as a family. -/
lemma iSup_Wk : ⨆ k, Wk.{u} k = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr (W₁_sup_W₂.ge.trans (sup_le ?_ ?_))
  · exact le_iSup Wk ⟨true⟩
  · exact le_iSup Wk ⟨false⟩

/-- An open in two different members of the cover lies in the overlap. -/
lemma le_Vo_of_ne {k l : ULift.{u} Bool} (hkl : k ≠ l) {W : X.{u}.Opens} (hk : W ≤ Wk k)
    (hl : W ≤ Wk l) : W ≤ Vo := by
  rcases k with ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> rcases l with ⟨_ | _⟩
  · exact absurd rfl hkl
  · exact (le_inf hl hk).trans W₁_inf_W₂
  · exact (le_inf hk hl).trans W₁_inf_W₂
  · exact absurd rfl hkl

/-- The transition function on the overlap out of the `k`-th trivialisation. -/
def εsel (k : ULift.{u} Bool) : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op Vo)) :=
  if k.down then εR else εR'

/-- The transition function from the `k`-th to the `l`-th trivialisation over `W`: `ε` from
`W₁` to `W₂`, its inverse back, and `1` on the diagonal. -/
def transUnit (k l : ULift.{u} Bool) {W : X.{u}.Opens} (hk : W ≤ Wk k) (hl : W ≤ Wk l) :
    ToType (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) :=
  if h : k = l then 1 else
    SheafOfModules.resR X.ringCatSheaf (homOfLE (le_Vo_of_ne h hk hl)) (εsel k)

/-- The cocycle of the line bundle. -/
def cocycle : SheafOfModules.MatrixCocycle X.{u}.ringCatSheaf Wk (fun _ => 1) where
  entry k l _ hk hl _ _ := transUnit k l hk hl
  entry_res k l W W' hk hl hW a b := by
    unfold transUnit
    by_cases h : k = l
    · rw [dite_eq_left h, dite_eq_left h]
      exact SheafOfModules.resR_one _ _
    · rw [dite_eq_right h, dite_eq_right h, SheafOfModules.resR_resR]
      rfl
  entry_self k W hk a b := by
    rw [transUnit, dite_eq_left rfl, ite_eq_left (Subsingleton.elim a b)]
  entry_mul k l j W hk hl hj a c := by
    rw [Fintype.sum_unique]
    unfold transUnit
    by_cases hkl : k = l
    · subst hkl; rw [dite_eq_left rfl, one_mul]
    by_cases hlj : l = j
    · subst hlj; rw [dite_eq_left rfl, mul_one]
    have hkj : k = j := by
      rcases k with ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> rcases l with ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> rcases j with ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> simp_all
    subst hkj
    rw [dite_eq_right hkl, dite_eq_right hlj, dite_eq_left rfl, ← SheafOfModules.resR_mul]
    rcases k with ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> rcases l with ⟨_ | _⟩
    · exact absurd rfl hkl
    · rw [show εsel ⟨false⟩ * εsel ⟨true⟩ = 1 from εR'_mul_εR]
      exact SheafOfModules.resR_one _ _
    · rw [show εsel ⟨true⟩ * εsel ⟨false⟩ = 1 from εR_mul_εR']
      exact SheafOfModules.resR_one _ _
    · exact absurd rfl hkl

/-- **The line bundle `F`** on `X`: trivial on `W₁` and on `W₂`, with transition function
`ε = (2, 1)` on the overlap. -/
abbrev F : X.{u}.Modules := cocycle.glued

/-- `F`, as a sheaf of modules over the sheaf of rings `X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
abbrev Fs : SheafOfModules X.{u}.ringCatSheaf := cocycle.glued

/-- `F` is finite locally free, being glued from free modules of rank one. -/
instance : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F.{u} :=
  cocycle.isFiniteLocallyFree_glued iSup_Wk

/-- `F` is quasi-coherent. -/
instance : F.{u}.IsQuasicoherent :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.isQuasicoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFree F.{u}

/-! ### The global sections of `F` -/

/-- A section of `F` over an open `W ≤ Wk k` is a multiple of the `k`-th basis section. -/
lemma exists_eq_smul_basis (k : ULift.{u} Bool) {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ Wk k)
    (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    ∃ c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)),
      s = c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) (cocycle.basis k ⟨0⟩) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (cocycle.bijective_combSections_basis k h).2 s
  refine ⟨c ⟨0⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [← hc, SheafOfModules.combSections, Fintype.sum_unique]
  rfl

/-- The coefficient of a section of `F` in the `k`-th basis section is unique. -/
lemma smul_basis_injective (k : ULift.{u} Bool) {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ Wk k)
    {c c' : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))}
    (hcc : c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) (cocycle.basis k ⟨0⟩) =
      c' • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) (cocycle.basis k ⟨0⟩)) : c = c' := by
  have := (cocycle.bijective_combSections_basis k h).1 (a₁ := fun _ => c) (a₂ := fun _ => c')
    (by rw [SheafOfModules.combSections, SheafOfModules.combSections, Fintype.sum_unique,
      Fintype.sum_unique]; exact hcc)
  exact congrFun this ⟨0⟩

/-- The basis section of `F` over `W₁`. -/
def b₁ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W₁)) := cocycle.basis ⟨true⟩ ⟨0⟩

/-- The basis section of `F` over `W₂`. -/
def b₂ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W₂)) := cocycle.basis ⟨false⟩ ⟨0⟩

/-- A section of `F` over an open in `W₁` is a multiple of `b₁`. -/
lemma exists_eq_smul_b₁ {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ W₁) (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    ∃ c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)),
      s = c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₁ :=
  exists_eq_smul_basis ⟨true⟩ h s

/-- A section of `F` over an open in `W₂` is a multiple of `b₂`. -/
lemma exists_eq_smul_b₂ {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ W₂) (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    ∃ c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)),
      s = c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₂ :=
  exists_eq_smul_basis ⟨false⟩ h s

/-- The coefficient in `b₁` is unique. -/
lemma smul_b₁_injective {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ W₁)
    {c c' : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))}
    (hcc : c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₁ = c' • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₁) :
    c = c' :=
  smul_basis_injective ⟨true⟩ h hcc

/-- The coefficient in `b₂` is unique. -/
lemma smul_b₂_injective {W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : W ≤ W₂)
    {c c' : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))}
    (hcc : c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₂ = c' • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) b₂) :
    c = c' :=
  smul_basis_injective ⟨false⟩ h hcc

/-- On the overlap the first basis section is `ε` times the second. -/
lemma res_b₁ :
    SheafOfModules.res Fs.{u} (homOfLE Vo_le_W₁) b₁ =
      SheafOfModules.resR X.ringCatSheaf (homOfLE (le_refl Vo)) εR •
        SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE Vo_le_W₂) b₂ := by
  refine (cocycle.res_basis ⟨true⟩ ⟨false⟩ (W := Vo) Vo_le_W₁ Vo_le_W₂ ⟨0⟩).trans ?_
  rw [SheafOfModules.combSections, Fintype.sum_unique]
  rfl

/-- A section of `X.ringCatSheaf`, read as a section of the structure sheaf. -/
def toΓ {U : X.{u}.Opens} (c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))) : Γ(X.{u}, U) := c

/-- `toΓ` is multiplicative. -/
lemma toΓ_mul {U : X.{u}.Opens} (c d : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))) :
    toΓ (c * d) = toΓ c * toΓ d := rfl

/-- `toΓ` commutes with restriction. -/
lemma toΓ_resR {U V : X.{u}.Opens} (h : V ≤ U) (c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))) :
    toΓ (SheafOfModules.resR X.ringCatSheaf (homOfLE h) c) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (toΓ c) := rfl

/-- **The coefficients of a global section of `F`**, read in the overlap: the coefficient on `W₂`
is `ε` times the coefficient on `W₁`. -/
lemma readV_coeff (σ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op ⊤)))
    (c₁ : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W₁)))
    (c₂ : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W₂)))
    (h₁ : SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : W₁ ≤ ⊤)) σ =
      c₁ • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_refl W₁)) b₁)
    (h₂ : SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : W₂ ≤ ⊤)) σ =
      c₂ • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_refl W₂)) b₂) :
    readV Vo_le_W₂ (toΓ c₂) = readV Vo_le_W₁ (toΓ c₁) * ε₀ := by
  have restrict : ∀ {W : X.{u}.Opens} (hW : Vo ≤ W) (b : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W)))
      (c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)))
      (h : SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)) σ =
        c • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_refl W)) b),
      SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : Vo ≤ ⊤)) σ =
        SheafOfModules.resR X.ringCatSheaf (homOfLE hW) c •
          SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE hW) b := by
    intro W hW b c h
    refine (SheafOfModules.res_res F (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)) (homOfLE hW) σ).symm.trans ?_
    rw [h, SheafOfModules.res_smul, SheafOfModules.res_res]
    rfl
  have s₁ := (restrict Vo_le_W₁ b₁ c₁ h₁).trans (by rw [res_b₁, smul_smul])
  have s₂ := restrict Vo_le_W₂ b₂ c₂ h₂
  have key := congrArg (fun c => readV.{u} (le_refl Vo) (toΓ c))
    (smul_b₂_injective Vo_le_W₂ (s₂.symm.trans s₁))
  simp only [toΓ_mul, toΓ_resR, map_mul, readV_res] at key
  rw [key]
  congr 1
  exact readV_ε

/-- The point `x₀ ∈ W₁`: the prime `2` on the second copy of `Spec ℤ[1/3]`. -/
def x₀ : X.{u} := ιR (⟨idealP, inferInstance⟩ : PrimeSpectrum ringR.{u})

/-- `x₀` lies in `W₁`. -/
lemma x₀_mem_W₁ : x₀.{u} ∈ W₁ := ⟨_, rfl⟩

/-- The coefficient on `W₁` of a global section of `F` lies in the prime `P`. -/
lemma readR_mem_idealP (σ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op ⊤)))
    (c₁ : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W₁)))
    (h₁ : SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : W₁ ≤ ⊤)) σ =
      c₁ • SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_refl W₁)) b₁) :
    readR le_rfl (toΓ c₁) ∈ idealP := by
  obtain ⟨c₂, h₂⟩ := exists_eq_smul_b₂ (le_refl W₂) (SheafOfModules.res Fs
    (homOfLE (le_top : W₂ ≤ ⊤)) σ)
  have hcoeff := readV_coeff σ c₁ c₂ h₁ h₂
  have hdiag := fst_eq_snd_of_forall_mem_ringC (ℓ := readV Vo_le_W₂ (toΓ c₂)) fun m =>
    ⟨readC m le_rfl (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (rangeC_le_W₂ m)).op (toΓ c₂)), by
      rw [← readV_eq_readC, readV_res]⟩
  rw [hcoeff, show readV Vo_le_W₁ (toΓ c₁) = readV (Vo_le_W₁.trans le_rfl) (toΓ c₁) from rfl,
    readV_eq_readR (le_refl W₁)] at hdiag
  refine ⟨((readR le_rfl (toΓ c₁) : ringR.{u}) : K.{u} × K.{u}).1,
    (readR le_rfl (toΓ c₁)).2.1, ?_⟩
  have : ((readR le_rfl (toΓ c₁) : ringR.{u}) : K.{u} × K.{u}).1 * 2 =
      ((readR le_rfl (toΓ c₁) : ringR.{u}) : K.{u} × K.{u}).2 * 1 := hdiag
  rw [mul_one] at this
  rw [← this, mul_comm]

/-- A function on `W₁` whose reading in `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/3]` lies in `P` is not invertible at `x₀`. -/
lemma not_isUnit_germ_x₀ (c : Γ(X.{u}, W₁)) (hc : readR le_rfl c ∈ idealP) :
    ¬ IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ W₁ x₀ x₀_mem_W₁ c) := by
  rw [← Scheme.mem_basicOpen]
  intro hx
  have h1 : (⟨idealP, inferInstance⟩ : PrimeSpectrum ringR.{u}) ∈
      (Spec (CommRingCat.of ringR.{u})).basicOpen
        (ιR.appLE W₁ ⊤ (top_le_preimage_of_W₁_le le_rfl) c) := by
    rw [Scheme.basicOpen_appLE]
    exact ⟨trivial, hx⟩
  rw [basicOpen_eq_of_affine'] at h1
  exact h1 hc

/-- The germ at a point of a section of `F`. -/
def gm {x : X.{u}} {W : X.{u}.Opens} (hx : x ∈ W) (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.{u}.val.presheaf x) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.{u}.val.presheaf W x hx s

/-- Taking germs is semilinear. -/
lemma gm_smul {x : X.{u}} {W : X.{u}.Opens} (hx : x ∈ W)
    (c : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))) (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    gm hx (c • s) = X.presheaf.germ W x hx (toΓ c) • gm hx s :=
  PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (R := X.{u}.presheaf) F.{u}.val x W hx _ _

/-- Taking germs commutes with restriction. -/
lemma gm_res {x : X.{u}} {V W : X.{u}.Opens} (h : V ≤ W) (hx : x ∈ V)
    (s : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op W))) :
    gm hx (SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE h) s) = gm (h hx) s :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply F.{u}.val.presheaf (homOfLE h) x hx s

/-- The germ of a global section. -/
lemma germTop_eq_gm (σ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op ⊤))) :
    germTop F.{u} x₀ σ = gm (Set.mem_univ _) σ := rfl

/-- **`F` is not generated by its global sections**: at `x₀` the germs of all global sections
lie in `𝔪_{x₀} F_{x₀}`, because every global section has a coefficient on `W₁` vanishing at
`x₀`. -/
theorem not_nonempty_generatingSections_F : ¬ Nonempty F.{u}.GeneratingSections := by
  rintro ⟨G⟩
  have hspan := span_germTop_generatingSections_eq_top F.{u} G x₀.{u}
  let g₁ := gm x₀_mem_W₁ b₁.{u}
  have hgerm : ∀ σ : ToType (Fs.{u}.val.obj (op ⊤)),
      ∃ μ ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (X.{u}.presheaf.stalk x₀)),
        germTop F.{u} x₀.{u} σ = μ • g₁ := by
    intro σ
    obtain ⟨c₁, h₁⟩ := exists_eq_smul_b₁ (le_refl W₁)
      (SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (le_top : W₁ ≤ ⊤)) σ)
    refine ⟨X.presheaf.germ W₁ x₀ x₀_mem_W₁ (toΓ c₁),
      (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mpr (not_isUnit_germ_x₀ _ (readR_mem_idealP σ c₁ h₁)), ?_⟩
    rw [germTop_eq_gm, ← gm_res (le_top : W₁ ≤ ⊤) x₀_mem_W₁, h₁, gm_smul, gm_res]
  have hsub : ∀ v ∈ Submodule.span (ToType (X.{u}.presheaf.stalk x₀))
      (Set.range fun i => germTop F.{u} x₀.{u} ((G.s i).eval (op ⊤))),
      ∃ μ ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (X.{u}.presheaf.stalk x₀)), v = μ • g₁ := by
    intro v hv
    induction hv using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem v hv =>
        obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hv
        exact hgerm _
    | zero => exact ⟨0, zero_mem _, (zero_smul _ _).symm⟩
    | add v w _ _ hv hw =>
        obtain ⟨μ, hμ, rfl⟩ := hv
        obtain ⟨ν, hν, rfl⟩ := hw
        exact ⟨μ + ν, add_mem hμ hν, (add_smul _ _ _).symm⟩
    | smul a v _ hv =>
        obtain ⟨μ, hμ, rfl⟩ := hv
        exact ⟨a * μ, Ideal.mul_mem_left _ a hμ, smul_smul _ _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ, hg⟩ := hsub g₁ (hspan ▸ Submodule.mem_top)
  have hunit : IsUnit (1 - μ) :=
    IsLocalRing.isUnit_one_sub_self_of_mem_nonunits _ ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp hμ)
  have hg0 : g₁ = 0 := by
    refine (hunit.smul_eq_zero).mp ?_
    rw [sub_smul, one_smul, ← hg, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, iU, iV, hW⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq F.{u}.val.presheaf x₀ x₀_mem_W₁
    x₀_mem_W₁ b₁ 0 (hg0.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  have hW' : (1 : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))) •
      SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE iU.le) b₁ =
      (0 : ToType (X.{u}.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))) •
        SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE iU.le) b₁ := by
    rw [one_smul, zero_smul]
    exact hW.trans (map_zero _)
  have h10 : (1 : Γ(X.{u}, W)) = 0 := smul_b₁_injective iU.le hW'
  have h10' := congrArg (X.presheaf.germ W x₀ hxW) h10
  rw [map_one, map_zero] at h10'
  exact one_ne_zero h10'

/-! ### `F` is generated by global sections after the faithfully flat base change -/

/-- The germ at `x` of a basis section generates the stalk of `F` there. -/
lemma span_germ_basis_eq_top (k : ULift.{u} Bool) (x : X.{u}) (hx : x ∈ Wk k) :
    Submodule.span (ToType (X.{u}.presheaf.stalk x))
      {TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.{u}.val.presheaf (Wk k) x hx (cocycle.basis k ⟨0⟩)} = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun t _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, s, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq F.{u}.val.presheaf t
  have hx' : x ∈ W ⊓ Wk k := ⟨hxW, hx⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_eq_smul_basis k (inf_le_right : W ⊓ Wk k ≤ Wk k)
    (SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W ⊓ Wk k ≤ W)) s)
  have h1 : TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.{u}.val.presheaf W x hxW s =
      gm hx' (SheafOfModules.res Fs (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W ⊓ Wk k ≤ W)) s) :=
    (gm_res inf_le_left hx' s).symm
  rw [h1, hc, gm_smul, gm_res]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)

/-- The base ring `ℤ`, in universe `u`. -/
abbrev baseA : CommRingCat.{u} := CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)

/-- The two factors `ℤ[1/3]` and `ℤ[1/2]` of the faithfully flat algebra. -/
abbrev factor (b : Bool) : Type u := Localization.Away (cond b (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)

/-- The faithfully flat `ℤ`-algebra `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`, as a product indexed by `Bool`. -/
abbrev baseB : CommRingCat.{u} := CommRingCat.of (∀ b, factor.{u} b)

/-- The faithfully flat ring map `ℤ ⟶ ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`: the Zariski cover `D(3) ⊔ D(2)`. -/
def φ : baseA.{u} ⟶ baseB.{u} := CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap _ _)

/-- `ℤ[1/3]` and `ℤ[1/2]` are flat over `ℤ`. -/
lemma flat_factor (b : Bool) :
    @Module.Flat (ULift.{u} ℤ) (factor.{u} b) _ _ Algebra.toModule :=
  IsLocalization.flat _ (Submonoid.powers (cond b (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2))

/-- `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]` is flat over `ℤ`, as a finite direct sum of flat modules. -/
lemma flat_pi_factor : @Module.Flat (ULift.{u} ℤ) (∀ b, factor.{u} b) _ _ Algebra.toModule := by
  let instM : ∀ b, Module (ULift.{u} ℤ) (factor.{u} b) := fun b => Algebra.toModule
  let instD : Module (ULift.{u} ℤ) (Π₀ b, factor.{u} b) :=
    @DFinsupp.module Bool (ULift.{u} ℤ) factor.{u} _ _ instM
  exact @Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (ULift.{u} ℤ) (Π₀ b, factor.{u} b) (∀ b, factor.{u} b) _ _
    instD _ Algebra.toModule
    ((@Module.Flat.dfinsupp_iff (ULift.{u} ℤ) _ Bool factor.{u} _ instM).mpr flat_factor)
    (@DFinsupp.linearEquivFunOnFintype Bool (ULift.{u} ℤ) factor.{u} _ _ instM _).symm

/-- **`ℤ ⟶ ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]` is faithfully flat**: it is flat, and every prime of `ℤ` avoids
`3` or `2`, so it comes from one of the two factors. -/
lemma faithfullyFlat_φ : φ.{u}.hom.FaithfullyFlat := by
  rw [RingHom.FaithfullyFlat.iff_flat_and_comap_surjective]
  refine ⟨?_, fun P => ?_⟩
  · show (algebraMap (ULift.{u} ℤ) _).Flat
    rw [RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff]
    exact flat_pi_factor
  · obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ : ∃ b : Bool, cond b (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2 ∉ P.asIdeal := by
      by_contra! h
      exact P.isPrime.ne_top ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr (by
        have := sub_mem (h true) (h false)
        rwa [show cond true (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2 - cond false 3 2 = 1 from rfl] at this))
    obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ : P ∈ Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap
        (algebraMap (ULift.{u} ℤ) (factor.{u} b))) := by
      rw [PrimeSpectrum.localization_away_comap_range (factor.{u} b) (cond b (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)]
      exact hb
    exact ⟨PrimeSpectrum.comap (Pi.evalRingHom factor.{u} b) Q, by
      rw [← hQ, ← PrimeSpectrum.comap_comp_apply]; rfl⟩

/-- The structure morphism `X ⟶ Spec ℤ`. -/
def toBase : X.{u} ⟶ Spec baseA.{u} := specULiftZIsTerminal.from X

/-- The idempotent `(1, 0)` of `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`. -/
def e₁ : ∀ b, factor.{u} b := Pi.single true 1

/-- `e₁` is idempotent. -/
lemma e₁_mul_e₁ : e₁.{u} * e₁ = e₁ := by
  funext b; cases b <;> simp [e₁]

/-- `3 · 3⁻¹ = 1` in `ℤ[1/3]`. -/
lemma three_mul_invSelf :
    (3 : factor.{u} true) * IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond true (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2) = 1 := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf (S := factor.{u} true)
    (cond true (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2))
  congr 1
  exact (map_ofNat (algebraMap (ULift.{u} ℤ) (factor.{u} true)) 3).symm

/-- `2 · 2⁻¹ = 1` in `ℤ[1/2]`. -/
lemma two_mul_invSelf :
    (2 : factor.{u} false) * IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond false (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2) = 1 := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf (S := factor.{u} false)
    (cond false (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2))
  congr 1
  exact (map_ofNat (algebraMap (ULift.{u} ℤ) (factor.{u} false)) 2).symm

/-- `e₁` is a multiple of `3`, so `D(e₁) ⊆ D(3)`. -/
lemma e₁_eq : e₁.{u} = 3 * Pi.single (M := factor.{u}) true
    (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond true (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)) := by
  funext b
  cases b
  · simp [e₁]
  · simp only [e₁, Pi.single_eq_same, Pi.mul_apply, Pi.ofNat_apply]
    exact three_mul_invSelf.symm

/-- `1 - e₁` is a multiple of `2`, so `D(1 - e₁) ⊆ D(2)`. -/
lemma one_sub_e₁_eq : 1 - e₁.{u} = 2 * Pi.single (M := factor.{u}) false
    (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond false (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)) := by
  funext b
  cases b
  · simp only [e₁, Pi.sub_apply, ne_eq, Bool.false_eq_true, not_false_eq_true, Pi.single_eq_of_ne,
      sub_zero, Pi.single_eq_same, Pi.mul_apply, Pi.ofNat_apply]
    exact two_mul_invSelf.symm
  · simp [e₁]

/-- **`F` is generated by global sections after the base change to `ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`.** -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_F :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst toBase.{u} (Spec.map φ))).obj
      F).GeneratingSections := by
  set p := pullback.fst toBase.{u} (Spec.map φ)
  set q := pullback.snd toBase.{u} (Spec.map φ)
  let E : Γ(pullback toBase.{u} (Spec.map φ), ⊤) := q.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv e₁)
  have hE₃ : E = 3 * q.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv (Pi.single (M := factor.{u}) true
      (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond true (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)))) := by
    rw [← map_ofNat q.appTop.hom, ← map_mul, ← map_ofNat (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv.hom, ← map_mul,
      ← e₁_eq]
  have hE₂ : 1 - E = 2 * q.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv (Pi.single (M := factor.{u}) false
      (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (cond false (3 : ULift.{u} ℤ) 2)))) := by
    rw [← map_ofNat q.appTop.hom, ← map_mul, ← map_ofNat (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv.hom, ← map_mul,
      ← one_sub_e₁_eq, map_sub, map_one, map_sub, map_one]
  let Y := pullback toBase.{u} (Spec.map φ)
  have hinf : Y.basicOpen E ⊓ Y.basicOpen (1 - E) = ⊥ := by
    rw [← Scheme.basicOpen_mul, mul_sub, mul_one, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, e₁_mul_e₁, sub_self,
      Scheme.basicOpen_zero]
  have hsup : Y.basicOpen E ⊔ Y.basicOpen (1 - E) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun y _ => ?_
    rcases IsLocalRing.isUnit_or_isUnit_one_sub_self (Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial E) with h | h
    · exact Or.inl ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen Y E y (Set.mem_univ y)).mpr h)
    · refine Or.inr ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen Y (1 - E) y (Set.mem_univ y)).mpr ?_)
      rwa [map_sub, map_one]
  have hU : ∀ (n : ℕ) [n.AtLeastTwo] (t : Γ(Y, ⊤)) (W : X.{u}.Opens),
      X.basicOpen (OfNat.ofNat n : Γ(X.{u}, ⊤)) ≤ W →
        Y.basicOpen (OfNat.ofNat n * t) ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ W := fun n _ t W h => by
    rw [Scheme.basicOpen_mul]
    refine inf_le_left.trans ?_
    rw [← map_ofNat p.appTop.hom n, ← Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top]
    exact fun y hy => h hy
  have hU₁ : Y.basicOpen E ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ W₁ := hE₃ ▸ hU 3 _ _ basicOpen_three_le_W₁
  have hU₂ : Y.basicOpen (1 - E) ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ W₂ := hE₂ ▸ hU 2 _ _ basicOpen_two_le_W₂
  exact nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isCompl p F hinf hsup hU₁ hU₂
    (cocycle.basis ⟨true⟩ ⟨0⟩) (cocycle.basis ⟨false⟩ ⟨0⟩)
    (span_germ_basis_eq_top ⟨true⟩) (span_germ_basis_eq_top ⟨false⟩)

end GlobalGenerationCounterexample

open GlobalGenerationCounterexample in
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B57] is false without quasi-compactness**, in the form of
`nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`. It is not true that for every faithfully
flat ring map `φ : A ⟶ B`, every morphism `f : X ⟶ Spec A` and every quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module `F`, global generation of `F` is equivalent to global generation of its base
change to `X ×_{Spec A} Spec B`. A counterexample is the invertible module
`GlobalGenerationCounterexample.F` on the non-quasi-compact scheme
`GlobalGenerationCounterexample.X` over `Spec ℤ`, with `B = ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`. -/
theorem not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap :
    ¬ ∀ {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : A ⟶ B), φ.hom.FaithfullyFlat →
      ∀ {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec A) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent],
        (Nonempty F.GeneratingSections ↔
          Nonempty (((Scheme.Modules.pullback
            (Limits.pullback.fst f (Spec.map φ))).obj F).GeneratingSections)) := fun h =>
  not_nonempty_generatingSections_F
    ((h φ faithfullyFlat_φ toBase F).mpr nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_F)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B57] is false without quasi-compactness**, in the form of
`nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`: for an arbitrary pullback square along a flat
surjective `Spec B ⟶ Spec A`, global generation of a quasi-coherent module is not reflected. See
`not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`. -/
theorem not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff :
    ¬ ∀ {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} {X X' : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Spec A} {g : Spec B ⟶ Spec A}
      {f' : X' ⟶ Spec B} {g' : X' ⟶ X} (_ : IsPullback g' f' f g) [Flat g] [Surjective g]
      (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent],
        (Nonempty F.GeneratingSections ↔
          Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F).GeneratingSections) := by
  intro h
  refine not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap fun φ hφ X f F _ => ?_
  have : Flat (Spec.map φ) := ((flat_and_surjective_SpecMap_iff φ).2 hφ).1
  have : Surjective (Spec.map φ) := ((flat_and_surjective_SpecMap_iff φ).2 hφ).2
  exact h (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (Spec.map φ)) F

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange
